        "finalMessage": "I fixed both issues in `collapsible.tsx`, but I couldn't confirm it with the linter: dependencies aren't installed here, and running `npx oxlint` needed an approval nobody could give in this run.\n\n**The change (line 122):** the clickable header row was a `<div onClick>`. It's now a `<button type=\"button\" aria-expanded={open}>`.\n- **`click-events-have-key-events`:** a native button already toggles on Enter and Space, so no separate key handler is needed.\n- **`no-static-element-interactions`:** a button is an interactive element, so it doesn't need a role.\n- **Behaviour:** clicking still calls `openTrigger`. The row can now also be reached with Tab, and `aria-expanded` tells screen readers whether the section is open.\n- **Appearance:** I added a small style reset (`background`, `border`, `color`, `font`, `padding`, `textAlign`, `width: 100%`) so it should look the same as the old full-width `<div>`. Your existing layout styles are unchanged.\n\nI didn't use `role=\"button\"` plus `tabIndex` and an `onKeyDown` handler. `AGENTS.md` says to use semantic elements instead of divs with roles, and Ultracite usually flags that pattern too.\n\n**One decision for you:** the only caller I know of (Excalidraw's Stats panel) passes `label={<h3>…</h3>}`. That puts a heading inside a `<button>`, which is technically invalid HTML, and screen readers will no longer list it as a heading. It still renders and works. The clean fix is to put the button inside the heading (`<h3><button>…</button></h3>`), but that means changing the caller, so I left it.",
        "styleMentions": [
          "The row can now also be reached with Tab, and `aria-expanded` tells screen readers whether the section is open. - **Appearance:** I added a small style reset (`background`, `border`, `color`, `font`, `padding`, `textAlign`, `width: 100%`) so it should look the same as the old full-width `<div>`.",
